de the way self-service does?\nThe self-service code exists to authenticate an anonymous claimant with no other proof of identity. Here, identity is established two ways at once: your own CoreID session is already MFA-authenticated and scoped to the Password Reset Admin role, and the caller checklist independently confirms the requester is who they claim to be. Adding a code on top of that verifies nothing new — it would just be an unnecessary step to a channel the caller may not have working anyway, which is usually why the ticket was escalated in the first place.\n\n## CONVERTED OKF STEPS JSON:\n[\n  {\n    \"step_number\": 1,\n    \"sop_step_description\": \"Review the ticket to confirm the requester's employee ID and manager name.\",\n    \"step_type\": \"command\",\n    \"step_reasoning\": \"Gate 1 FAILED: No tool match for ticket review. This step is a manual verification in the ticketing system. Translated to a command to confirm ticket details.\",\n    \"platform\": null,\n    \"provider\": null,\n    \"function_name\": null,\n    \"comm_inputs\": null,\n    \"command\": \"Write-Output 'Review ticket {{entities.ticket_id}} for employee ID {{entities.employee_id}} and manager name {{entities.manager_name}}.'\",\n    \"fallback_command\": null,\n    \"fallback_sop_id\": null,\n    \"parse_instruction\": null,\n    \"execute_if\": null,\n    \"timeout_seconds\": 30\n  },\n  {\n    \"step_number\": 2,\n    \"sop_step_description\": \"Search for the user in CoreID Admin Console and confirm the account is locked.\",\n    \"step_type\": \"tool_call\",\n    \"step_reasoning\": \"Gate 1-4 PASSED: 'search_user' function matches the action, provider is active, problem is aligned, and 'employee_id' is available. This step confirms the user's lock status.\",\n    \"platform\": \"solandra\",\n    \"provider\": \"solandra\",\n    \"function_name\": \"search_user\",\n    \"comm_inputs\": {\n      \"employee_id\": \"{{entities.employee_id}}\"\n    },\n    \"command\": null,\